<title>SWITZERLAND: Selecta starts trading at 211 Swiss francs.</title>
<headline>Selecta starts trading at 211 Swiss francs.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Registered shares of Swiss vending machine retailer Selecta began trading at 211 Swiss francs, above the 206 Swiss franc issue price for the stock offer. Prices were steady in early business.</p>
<p>The shares were launched on Swiss and London bourses.</p>
<p>A majority stake in the company was floated by parent Swiss kiosk, speciality shop and bedding store chain Valora, which changed its name last year from Merkur. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
